WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.142
Step 1. Open the charge item definitions.

1.2
00:00:03.142 --> 00:00:08.785
Taxes and discounts set on a category apply to every definition in it and in its

1.3
00:00:08.785 --> 00:00:14.504
subcategories. In Settings, under Billing, select Charge Item Definitions.

2.1
00:00:14.504 --> 00:00:19.980
Step 2. Find the category. Care shows the top-level categories as cards.

2.2
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:25.198
If the category is a subcategory, open its parent category first.

3.1
00:00:25.198 --> 00:00:29.164
Step 3. Open the monetary components of the category.

3.2
00:00:29.164 --> 00:00:34.914
On its card, select the menu button with three dots, then Set Monetary Components.

3.3
00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:39.060
The sheet shows the taxes and discounts already set.

4.1
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:41.261
Step 4. Select the taxes.

4.2
00:00:41.261 --> 00:00:47.502
Under Taxes, select the box, then select the check box of each tax that applies.

4.3
00:00:47.502 --> 00:00:48.938
Select Done.

5.1
00:00:48.938 --> 00:00:55.096
Step 5. Select the discounts. Select each discount that applies, then select Done.

5.2
00:00:55.096 --> 00:01:01.289
For each one, use the facility global value, or override it with a local value.

6.1
00:01:01.289 --> 00:01:05.294
Step 6. Save the taxes and discounts. Select Save.

6.2
00:01:05.294 --> 00:01:11.304
If a subcategory or a definition has its own tax or discount with the same code,

6.3
00:01:11.304 --> 00:01:13.832
Care uses that one instead.
